## M2 survived the first run, and the test was the thing at fault
The first FI2 only had fixtures with a NON-EMPTY iv_best, so a resolver keyed on the source string still passed it.
The fixture that matters is an EMPTY iv_best with an exact-looking source (structure_steady): a string-keyed resolver
calls it EXACT with iv None. Asserting only that gate_interval raises would NOT have caught it either, because it still
raises - on 'not in the allowed set', the wrong reason. FI2 now asserts the TIER. A green battery with a surviving
mutation is a hole in the battery, not a property of the code.
